    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Self-attested RC photocopy:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">A photocopy of the Registration Certificate (RC) for the motorcycle is crucial. This document is issued by the Regional Transport Office (RTO) and proves the ownership of the vehicle. Ensure that the copy is self-attested to avoid any complications during the transportation process.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Proof of pollution control (PUC) is essential for bike transportation. A PUC certificate confirms that the motorcycle meets emission standards and is in good condition. Make sure to get a fresh PUC before the transportation process.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid insurance certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Proof of insurance is mandatory for any vehicle transportation. Ensure that the motorcycle is insured and that the insurance certificate is up-to-date to avoid any legal issues during transportation.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA-approved consignment bill of lading:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The Indian Bureau of Mines (IBA) has approved a consignment bill of lading for efficient and safe transportation of goods, including motorcycles. This document serves as a contract between the transporter and the vehicle owner, detailing the terms and conditions of the transportation process.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p><strong>100% Declared-Value Marine Transit Insurance:</strong></p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
  <li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>100% declared-value marine transit insurance ensures that the motorcycle is fully insured during the transportation process. This type of insurance covers the motorcycle for any damage or loss that may occur during transportation, providing peace of mind to the vehicle owner.</span></li>
</ul>

<p>Before proceeding with the transportation, ensure that the bike is in good condition, with all necessary documents up-to-date and in order.</p>

<p>When hiring a transporter, ensure they provide a bill of lading (IBA-approved) that includes the declared value of the motorcycle. This will ensure that the motorcycle is insured for its full value, in case of any damages or accidents during transportation.</p>

<p>Additionally, it's important to have photocopies of the bike's RC, PUC, insurance certificate, and the bill of lading readily available for the transporter.</p>

<p>Make sure to communicate your expectations clearly, such as the mode of transportation (road, rail, or air) and the mode of transport (open or enclosed trailer).</p>

<p>Before the transportation begins, inspect the motorcycle for any damages or defects and document them on the bill of lading for future reference.</p>

<p>Upon receiving the motorcycle at the destination, inspect the motorcycle again for any damages or discrepancies.</p>

<p>In case of any damages or discrepancies, document them on the bill of lading and contact the transporter immediately to resolve the issue.</p>

<p>By following these guidelines and ensuring all necessary paperwork is in order, you can have a smooth and stress-free bike transportation experience in Nagarjunakonda.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


